  "imagePrompt": "A high-quality, detailed illustration designed for an IELTS or Eiken English speaking picture-description test. Show a lively Japanese summer festival in the evening, filled with colorful lanterns, food stalls, festival games, families, and people wearing casual summer clothes and yukata. The main event should be clear in the foreground: a young boy around six years old is standing alone near a festival walkway, looking frightened and close to tears because he has become separated from his family. A female security staff member wearing a simple festival security vest is crouching down beside him and speaking gently to reassure him. The boy is holding a small festival bag and looking around nervously. In the middle distance, his worried mother is searching through the crowd, calling and looking in different directions, clearly trying to find him. Include several clear background sub-stories. On the left, a young child has accidentally dropped a red candy apple onto the ground and looks disappointed while a parent reacts with surprise. Nearby, a boy at a goldfish-scooping stall has accidentally knocked over a small container of water and is trying to stop the spill. On the right, a woman wearing a yukata is sitting on a bench trying to fix a broken sandal while her friend helps her. At another food stall, a vendor is quickly catching a stack of trays or boxes that is about to fall. In the far background, several visitors are looking up happily at fireworks in the night sky, while others continue walking through the crowded festival. Include lanterns, food stalls, festival games, benches, shopping bags, signs with simple decorative symbols, and colorful festival decorations. Make all actions and emotions visually distinct and easy to describe. Clear foreground, middle ground, and background, approximately 10 to 14 visible people. No speech bubbles, no captions, no logos, no copyrighted characters, no text required to understand the image. Landscape 16